AI: 
                                   Root Cause                                   

Port mismatch causing health probe failures. Redis is configured to listen on   
port 9999 (via --port 9999 args) but liveness and readiness probes check port   
6379, causing continuous probe failures and pod restarts.                       


                                    Evidence                                    

Deployment config:                                                              

 • Container args: --port 9999                                                  
 • Liveness probe: tcp-socket :6379                                             
 • Readiness probe: tcp-socket :6379                                            

Pod events (last 30 min):                                                       

                                                                                
 Liveness probe failed: dial tcp 10.244.0.34:6379: connect: connection refused  
 Readiness probe failed: dial tcp 10.244.0.34:6379: connect: connection refused 
                                                                                

Pod status:                                                                     

 • State: CrashLoopBackOff (11 restarts)                                        
 • Redis starts successfully on port 9999, then Kubernetes kills it after 15s   
   when probes fail                                                             

Logs: Redis initializes correctly and is "Ready to accept connections tcp" but  
receives SIGTERM from kubelet due to failed probes.                             


                                      Fix                                       

Remove the --port 9999 args from the deployment (Redis defaults to 6379):       

                                                                                
 kubectl patch deployment redis-cart -n boutique --type=json -p='[{"op":        
 "remove", "path": "/spec/template/spec/containers/0/args"}]'                   
                                                                                

Or update probes to match port 9999 if that port is required.                   
