AI: 
                       Root Cause: Port Misconfiguration                        

Pod redis-cart-6696998457-dss7g is in CrashLoopBackOff due to a port mismatch   
between Redis startup and health probes.                                        

The Problem:                                                                    

 • Redis is configured to start with --port 9999 (deployment args)              
 • Liveness and readiness probes check port 6379 (default Redis port)           
 • Redis starts successfully on port 9999 but probes fail on 6379               
 • Failed probes trigger container restarts (11 restarts so far)                

Evidence:                                                                       

                                                                                
 Args: --port 9999                                                              
 Liveness:  tcp-socket :6379                                                    
 Readiness: tcp-socket :6379                                                    
                                                                                

Logs show Redis starts cleanly ("Ready to accept connections tcp") then receives
SIGTERM from Kubernetes after probe failures.                                   

Fix: Update the deployment to either:                                           

 1 Remove the --port 9999 args (use default 6379), OR                           
 2 Change probes to check port 9999                                             

                                                                                
 kubectl patch deployment redis-cart -n boutique --type='json' -p='[{"op":      
 "remove", "path": "/spec/template/spec/containers/0/args"}]'                   
                                                                                
