AI: 
                                   Root Cause                                   

redis-cart deployment has a port configuration mismatch causing                 
readiness/liveness probe failures.                                              

The Problem:                                                                    

 • Redis container starts with --port 9999 argument (listens on port 9999)      
 • Readiness/liveness probes check port 6379                                    
 • Probes fail with connection refused → pod never becomes Ready → deployment   
   shows 0/1 available replicas                                                 

Evidence:                                                                       

 • Deployment spec: args: ["--port", "9999"]                                    
 • Probes: tcpSocket: {port: 6379}                                              
 • Pod events: Readiness probe failed: dial tcp 10.244.0.34:6379: connect:      
   connection refused                                                           
 • Redis logs: Ready to accept connections tcp (on port 9999)                   
 • Pod status: Running but not Ready (0/1), 13 restarts                         

Fix: Remove the --port 9999 argument from the deployment to let Redis use       
default port 6379:                                                              

                                                                                
 kubectl patch deployment redis-cart -n boutique --type=json -p='[{"op":        
 "remove", "path": "/spec/template/spec/containers/0/args"}]'                   
                                                                                

Or update probes to check port 9999 instead (less recommended as it breaks      
service expectations).                                                          
