AI: 
                              Root Cause Analysis                               

Alert: BoutiqueServiceDown - cartservice has 0 available replicas               

Primary Root Cause: cartservice pod is being OOMKilled (Out of Memory). The     
container exceeds its 128Mi memory limit and gets terminated by Kubernetes (Exit
Code 137).                                                                      

Secondary Root Cause: redis-cart dependency is misconfigured. Redis is          
configured to listen on port 9999 (--port 9999 arg) but liveness/readiness      
probes check port 6379, causing continuous probe failures and restarts.         

                                   Evidence:                                    

 1 cartservice OOMKilled:                                                       
    • Pod cartservice-9479b6c-mg7ls status: Last State: Terminated, Reason:     
      OOMKilled, Exit Code: 137                                                 
    • Memory limit: 128Mi (too low for workload)                                
    • 8 restarts due to repeated OOM kills                                      
    • Liveness probes timing out because container crashes before becoming      
      healthy                                                                   
 2 redis-cart port mismatch:                                                    
    • Redis starts with --port 9999 but probes check port 6379                  
    • Liveness probe: tcp-socket :6379 (fails with "connection refused")        
    • Redis logs show successful startup on port 9999, then SIGTERM from failed 
      probes                                                                    
    • 13 restarts in CrashLoopBackOff                                           

                                      Fix:                                      

 1 Increase cartservice memory limit:                                           
                                                                                
    kubectl set resources deployment cartservice -n boutique                    
    --limits=memory=256Mi                                                       
                                                                                
 2 Fix redis-cart port configuration (choose one):                              
    • Remove --port 9999 arg to use default port 6379, OR                       
    • Update probes to check port 9999:                                         
                                                                                
    kubectl patch deployment redis-cart -n boutique --type=json                 
    -p='[{"op":"remove","path":"/spec/template/spec/containers/0/args"}]'       
                                                                                
