AI: 
                  Root Cause: OOMKilled - Memory Limit Too Low                  

Pod cartservice-9479b6c-mg7ls in namespace boutique is crash looping because the
container is being killed by the OOM (Out of Memory) killer.                    

                                    Evidence                                    

From pod description:                                                           

                                                                                
 Last State:     Terminated                                                     
   Reason:       OOMKilled                                                      
   Exit Code:    137                                                            
                                                                                

The container repeatedly exceeds its memory limit and gets killed, triggering   
CrashLoopBackOff.                                                               

                              Configuration Issue                               

Memory limits are too restrictive:                                              

 • Memory Limit: 128Mi                                                          
 • Memory Request: 64Mi                                                         

The cartservice application is processing cart operations (GetCartAsync calls   
visible in logs) and health checks, but the 128Mi limit is insufficient for the 
workload, causing the kernel OOM killer to terminate the container.             

                                      Fix                                       

Increase memory limits in the deployment:                                       

                                                                                
 kubectl set resources deployment cartservice -n boutique \                     
   --limits=memory=256Mi \                                                      
   --requests=memory=128Mi                                                      
                                                                                

Or edit the deployment directly:                                                

                                                                                
 kubectl edit deployment cartservice -n boutique                                
                                                                                

And adjust:                                                                     

                                                                                
 resources:                                                                     
   limits:                                                                      
     memory: 256Mi  # or higher based on actual usage                           
   requests:                                                                    
     memory: 128Mi                                                              
                                                                                

Monitor actual memory usage with kubectl top pod -n boutique to determine       
optimal limits.                                                                 
